WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.450
This rule matters because it gives
people permission not to meet.

2
00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:08.275
It's the guide's own design guidance for
the program, built on those two sources.

3
00:00:08.275 --> 00:00:12.188
If information only needs to flow
one way, send a written update,

4
00:00:12.188 --> 00:00:15.875
and meet only if the questions
really need live discussion.

5
00:00:15.875 --> 00:00:18.795
If there's a problem to
work or a decision to make,

6
00:00:18.795 --> 00:00:22.987
that's what meetings are for, so meet,
with the right people in the room.

7
00:00:22.987 --> 00:00:26.113
And give every recurring
meeting a check once a quarter.

8
00:00:26.113 --> 00:00:29.533
One that no longer decides
anything should be cancelled,

9
00:00:29.533 --> 00:00:31.425
or turned into a written report.

10
00:00:31.425 --> 00:00:35.400
Once you've decided to meet, the next
question is what kind of meeting it is.
